","The REVISIONIST, who was the plaintiff-appellant, filed this revision under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the judgment and decree dated 04.09.2002 of the learned appellate court, which affirmed the decree dated 17.11.1990 of the learned trial court disposing of his title suit of 1987 against OPPOSITE PARTY No. 1, the Airport Manager, and OPPOSITE PARTY No. 2. He sought declaration of title to the suit land, claiming its predecessor-in-title took a settlement in 1935-36, that the land was requisitioned during the Second World War and derequisitioned in 1952, and that he acquired it under two registered deeds of 1987. The OPPOSITE PARTY relied on transfer and acquisition in favour of the Civil Aviation Authority in 1957-58 and on the MRR and BS records. The REVISIONIST urged that records of rights create no title and are mere evidence of possession.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"Nobody appeared for the REVISIONIST to support the Rule, yet the court examined the lower court records. It found that the suit was founded on proof of title and possession, a burden the REVISIONIST bore and did not discharge: his witnesses gave inconsistent statements and produced no document establishing title, possession or any objection to the records of rights, which were never challenged. The OPPOSITE PARTY's witnesses, by contrast, produced the wartime requisition and the acquisition in favour of the Civil Aviation Authority. Both courts below having on the evidence reached concurrent findings, the court held that no error of law causing failure of justice was shown and that no case for interference arose.",8771be66d4fc83018f786628acc92daac19f30d39258252dc1e55ae880af3852
