A.K.M.Asaduzzaman,J. 
 
This Rule Nisi was issued calling upon the respondents to show 
cause as to why inaction and failure of the respondents in not 
publishing full result and also not appointing the petitioners in the 

<<PAGE 2>>
 
2
vacant post of Cadet Sub-Inspector (unarmed) should not be declared to 
have been made without lawful authority and is of no legal effect. 
 
During pendency of the rule on 15.05.2024 a further direction 
was given to the respondents to reserve the 88(eighty eight) Cadet Sub-
Inspector (unarmed) posts vacant for the applicant–petitioners for a 
period of 06(six) months from date.    
Fact relevant for disposal of this rule are that on 04.05.2023 
respondent No. 3 published an advertisement seeking for applications 
from the aspirants for direct recruitment in the vacant post of Cadet 
Sub-Inspector (unarmed) of Bangladesh Police.  The petitioners having 
found themselves eligible and with a view to serve the nation, 
submitted applications and successfully passed preliminary screening 
and physical Endurance Test (PET). After having successfully 
completed Physical Endurance Test (PET) the petitioners were 
qualified for written and psychological test. Accordingly, the 
petitioners appeared in and passed written and psychological test of 
which result published on 30.07.2023. Thereafter the petitioners sat in 
Computer Competency Test and successfully passed the Computer 
Competency Test. The petitioners passed preliminary Screening, 
Physical Endurance Test (PET), written and psychological test, 
Computer Competency Test and finally qualified for Aptitude Test and 
Viva-Voce Test and they appeared in the Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce 

<<PAGE 3>>
 
3
Test held on different dates. Respondents vide letter in Memo Nathi 
No. 44.01.0000.028.01.016.23.1625 dated 13.10.2023 published the 
result of Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce Test recommending only 921 
candidates for appointment as against the vacant post of more or less 
1400 vacant post. There are as many as 1400 post of Sub-Inspector 
(unarmed) are vacant throughout the country. After the candidates 
finally got recommendation, they have to take strict physical and 
fundamental test yearlong in Bangladesh Police Academy Sardah. But 
for lack of accommodation facilities in Sardah, the selection committee 
recommended only 921 candidates as against about 1400 vacant post 
which would be evident from paper clippings of different reputed 
national dailies. The petitioners filed written representations with the 
respondents seeking for publishing the result of Aptitude Test and Viva 
Voce Test so far as the petitioners could know their position in merit 
list but the respondents did not take any positive step on the basis of the 
petitioners representations.  
It is further mentioned that though the result of Aptitude Test 
and Viva Voce Test selecting only 921 candidates for appointment as 
against the vacant post of more or less 1400 vacant post was passed, 
but only 815 joined in Bangladesh Police Academy, Sardah to take year 
long physical and fundamental test and after year long training figure of 
eligible candidates must come down heavily for appointment. On 

<<PAGE 4>>
 
4
30.11.2023 petitioners filed a representation with the respondents 
requesting them to fill up the vacant post of Cadet Sub-Inspector 
(unarmed) but the respondents did not take any positive action on the 
basis of the petitioners representation.  
Challenging the said in action as well as not publishing the final 
result of the viva-voce, Aptitude Test as well as not giving the selection 
to the petitioners arbitrarily and give a pick and choose selection. 
Petitioners being aggrieved moved this writ petition and obtained the 
instant rule.  
Mr. Md. Monirul Islam Miah, the learned advocate appearing 
for the petitioners submits that although petitioners were successfully 
come out from Preliminary Screening Test, Physical Endurance Test 
(PET), Written and Psychological Test, Computer Competency Test 
and finally qualified for Aptitude Test and Viva-voce test and they  
appeared in the viva-voce test  with different test in different dates but 
due to lack of accommodation facilities in Sardah, a selection 
committee recommended only 921 candidates as against  1400 vacant 
posts, the writ petitioners being the eligible candidates ought to have 
allowed. Subsequently with recommendation to have strict physical and 
fundamental test year long training in Bangladesh Police Academy, 
Sardah, Despite that the respondents most illegally kept mum and not 
responding to the petitioners representation thereby devoid their 

<<PAGE 5>>
 
5
Fundamental rights. Impugned in action is apparently illegal and not 
sustainable in law, which is liable to be declared without any lawful 
authority and is of no legal effect. Learned advocate further submits 
that when there are already a lot of vacant post are there and the 
petitioners have successfully passed all tests and pre-qualification 
needed to be obtained an order of appointment in the police service, 
inspite of that by ignoring their legal claim respondents violated their 
fundamental rights. He finally prays for making the rule absolute and a 
proper order of recommendation for their appointment in service.  
On the other hand, Government opposed the rule by filing an 
affidavit in opposition on behalf of the respondent no. 4. Learned 
Deputy Attorney General in support of his affidavit in opposition 
submits that Annexure G of the writ petition, a final publication of the 
result of the Aptitude Test and Viva Voce Test vide memo no. 
44.01.0000.028.01.016.23.1625 dated 13.10.2023 publishing the result 
of 921 candidates, clearly shows that they are only passed the Aptitude 
Test and Viva Voce Test and petitioners since not passed the said test, 
their names were not published in the said result. Since the petitioners 
could not succeed the Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce Test, they are not 
eligible to get any appointment or any recommendation for having year 
long training in the Bangladesh Police Academy, Sardah, even if there 

<<PAGE 6>>
 
6
are lot of vacancy are there in the police force. Since the rule contains 
no merits, it may be discharged.  
Heard the learned advocate of both the sides and perused the 
document annexed to the writ petition and supplementary affidavit and  
the affidavit in opposition.  
Admittedly petitioners appeared before the Preliminary 
Screening and Physical Endurance Test (PET) pursuant to their 
application on the advertisement dated 04.05.2023 and thereafter being 
qualified appeared before the written and Psychological test and 
subsequently on Computer Competency Test and successfully passed 
their all test there and finally qualified for Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce 
Test. Thereafter by the impugned order dated 13.10.2023, result was 
published on Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce Test recommending only 
921 candidates  for appointment as against the vacant post of more or 
less 1400vacant posts. Now at present there are lot of vacant post in the 
country, which would be evident from paper clippings on different 
national dailies. Although the result of Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce 
Test shows only 921 candidates were passed but only 815 candidates 
join in Bangladesh Police Academy, Sardah to take year long physical 
and fundamental test. After the July Revolution, the police force has 
already been seriously damaged and there are lot of scarcity of police 
personnel in the country thereby law and order situation of the country 

<<PAGE 7>>
 
7
is under threat and thus at present there are very urgent need to get 
more police force in the Bangladesh police. Since the petitioners are 
already have passed their almost all examination including the written 
test but only could not succeed in the Aptitude Test and Viva-Voce 
Test that may be taken into a lenient view for them to allow them to get 
their appointment as well as to have their to have a recommendation to 
have their year long physical and fundamental test at Sardah for the 
interest of the country. Moreover, out of the present petitioner 
maximum candidates are already expired their eligible period for 
getting government service and they are not in a position to apply 
further for any job in future. Considering this, on humanity ground, we 
can also get a concessional view to have their job in the police service.  
In the premises, in action of respondents for not responding their 
representation appears to be taken without any lawful authority.  
We thus find merits in this rule.  
Accordingly the rule is made absolute. 
 The inaction/failure of the respondents in not publishing the full 
result as well as not appointing the petitioners in vacant post of Cadet 
Sub-Inspector (unarmed) of Bangladesh Police is hereby declared to 
have been done without lawful authority and is of no legal effect. 
Respondents are hereby directed to take all necessary steps to give 

<<PAGE 8>>
 
8
appoint the petitioners to the vacant post of Cadet Sub-Inspector 
(unarmed) of Bangladesh Police immediately.            
Communicate the judgment at once.  
 
Syed Enayet Hossain, J: 
  
 
 
 
 
I agree. 
","The PETITIONERS, aspirants recruited by open advertisement dated 04.05.2023 for direct appointment as Cadet Sub-Inspector (unarmed) in the police force, filed this writ petition under Article 102 of the Constitution against the STATE and the appointing authorities, challenging the inaction in publishing the full result of the recruitment and in appointing them to the roughly fourteen hundred vacant posts. They recounted clearing preliminary screening, the physical endurance, written, psychological and computer competency stages, and sitting the aptitude and viva-voce tests, when only nine hundred and twenty-one candidates were recommended, a shortfall they attributed to shortage of accommodation at the academy; their representations of 30.11.2023 and thereafter drew no reply. A Rule Nisi issued with directions reserving eighty-eight posts for six months. The STATE answers that the petitioners failed the aptitude and viva-voce test and so are ineligible.","Constitution of Bangladesh, Article 102",ALLOWED,"The court recorded that the petitioners had qualified at every earlier stage, that only 921 were recommended against about 1400 vacancies owing to shortage of academy accommodation, and that of these only 815 joined the year-long training. It weighed the reduced strength of the police force after the July events as making immediate recruitment urgent, and treated failure at the aptitude and viva-voce stage alone as calling for a lenient and concessional approach, reinforced by humanity, since most petitioners had passed the age limit for service and could not apply again. The inaction was held without lawful authority, so the Rule was made absolute with a direction to appoint.",cb97db282e46ea9a45d10bac9c4f08138769d75f673a964955a285ad15b5791c
