","The REVISIONISTS, plaintiffs in a partition suit, moved this revision under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the judgment and order dated 15.06.2023 of the learned District Judge in Miscellaneous Appeal No. 11 of 2023, which affirmed the order dated 12.02.2023 of the learned trial court in Title Suit No. 906 of 2021 granting their OPPOSITE PARTIES, defendants in that suit, a temporary injunction. The REVISIONISTS maintained that the injunction had been improperly obtained and that the appellate order proceeded without due appreciation of their objections, while the OPPOSITE PARTIES defended the order as lawful. A Rule Nisi issued, and the parties were directed to preserve the status quo as to possession and position of the suit property, that direction subsisting for more than eighteen months.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"UNCERTAIN: the judgment gives no reasoning of its own on the merits of the injunction, rests instead on elapsed delay and the pending suit, and records the rule as disposed of without saying whether the challenge succeeds, so the outcome is inferred. The court directed the trial court to hear and decide the title suit strictly on merit, applying an independent judicial mind, within six months without adjournment, and to report disposal in writing through the Registrar within seven days. The direction to maintain the status quo, in force since 2023, was continued for that period, leaving the injunction the REVISIONISTS assailed in place while the main suit awaits decision.",06fbd1823d744ed380ec74c1ffe0f4b18eed74267d232c7e5a5acfb45c4fd0f3
