","The REVISIONISTS, heirs of contesting defendants, moved this revision under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the decree dated 08.02.2021 of the learned District Judge, which affirmed the decree dated 30.09.2018 of the learned trial court decreeing the OPPOSITE PARTIES' suit of 2013 for permanent injunction over one acre within a plot of some nineteen acres. The injunction suit was framed on settlement of Government land recorded in Khatian No. 1 by registered kabul in 1975, a transfer by gift for consideration in 1991 and a kabala of later that year, with user by a tank and dwelling huts. The REVISIONISTS claimed through a kabala of 1963 and successive transfers, denied that the acre was Government land, urged that no certified copy of that khatian was ever produced, and relied on admissions of the third plaintiff in cross-examination.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court held that, the Government's title to the acre being denied, the plaintiffs had to establish a prima facie case; yet only the defendants' khatian, showing 1.26 acres of the plot, stood before the court, the survey record being accepted without a certified copy of Khatian No. 1, which also belied the plea that the whole plot stood in the Government's name. On possession, the first witness admitted holding over 84 decimals only, with a road and his nephew's hut elsewhere, and the second placed his own house and tank on the land, so user of the whole acre was unestablished. An admission is evidence against its maker, and injunction could not reach what the plaintiffs did not possess.",a96bd57e43e1aa21a774258b8a9fcc3a3df36ab19b1c609a86105d92e0e222cb
