","The PETITIONER, appellant in Title Appeal No. 12 of 2022 before the learned District Judge, Khulna, preferred revision under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the order dated 05.01.2023 in that appeal, whereby, the appeal being ready for hearing, the appellate court declined to hear separately his application for temporary injunction and directed both sides to prepare for the appeal itself, and obtained a Rule together with an order of status quo. Before this Court his learned Advocate was unable to advance anything contrary to the submissions of the learned Advocate appearing for OPPOSITE PARTY Nos. 1-6, the zonal and local offices of the housing finance corporation, who relied on the record of the appeal.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court ascertained that during the pendency of the Rule Title Appeal No. 12 of 2022 had been finally disposed of by the judgment and decree dated 24.08.2023, the appeal having met contest and failed, a copy of that decree having been submitted by the learned Advocate for the opposite parties. The grievance, that the appellate court declined to hear the injunction application separately, therefore survived no live question, the proceeding in which protection was sought having itself ended. Nothing useful remained to be ordered, and the court recorded that the Rule had become infructuous. The Rule was discharged, without any order as to costs, and the status quo vacated.",069156a3b3675ba528f77e5c68629f6f016e0ec104e68a8bd2aad3031123e2eb
