","The APPELLANT, convicted and sentenced by the learned Nari-O-Shishu Nirjatan Daman Tribunal No. 01, Naogaon, preferred this appeal before the High Court Division; his learned Advocate sought the leave of this Court to have it heard, the sentence having included a fine of which recovery is pending, and asked to be enlarged on bail until the appeal is disposed of. The STATE was represented by the learned Deputy Advocate General and puisne Advocates-General, and nothing in the record discloses that the respondents were heard on the application.",Other: Code of Criminal Procedure 1898,ALLOWED,"NOT_STATED. The order is confined to the operative directions, namely that the appeal will be heard, records be called for, the usual notices issue upon the respondents and the preparation of the paper book be dispensed with. Recovery of the fine is stayed pending hearing, and the APPELLANT is enlarged on bail for six months from the date, on furnishing a bail bond to the satisfaction of the trial Tribunal, no reasons being assigned: the whole issues as one operative order.",e3530460ce4e73b50471f95b9787c1f02b34b5faabbffcac359658138d3329f1
