Arif, ABO 
","The PRE-EMPTTEE-PETITIONER, who bought 1.20 acre in S. A. Khatian No. 822 of Golokpur under Tajumuddin in Bhola by registered sale deed No. 461 of 22.03.1997 as a stranger to the jote, obtained a Rule against the order dated 09.06.2010 of the learned Additional District Judge, Bhola, in Pre-emption Miscellaneous Appeal No. 18 of 2006, which left standing the judgment and decree of the learned Joint District Judge, 2nd Court, Bhola, dated 20.07.2006 in Pre-emption Miscellaneous Case No. 16 of 1997, the PRE-EMPTOR having claimed as a co-sharer in that khatian on a case filed on 15.09.1997. He presses one ground, that the PRE-EMPTOR, holding 108 decimals of the same khatian by a separate mutation made long before the case, ceased to be a co-sharer under section 117(1)(c) of the State Acquisition and Tenancy Act 1950, unseen by both courts; no opposite party appeared.",State Acquisition and Tenancy Act 1950,ALLOWED,"Exhibit-1, the PRE-EMPTOR's own tender, was a mutation khatian, though he called it part of the S. A. Khatian, and showed a separate khatian opened in his name for 108 decimals by order dated 21.10.1989 in Mutation Case No. 61 (part 2) of 1989-90, so the jama stood subdivided at his own instance before his case. The court applied 18 DLR 281, 33 DLR (AD) 305 and 309 and 55 DLR 214, under which one ceasing to be a co-sharer on separation cannot pre-empt on that footing, subsisting interest being needed from filing until disposal, while a separation by a competent revenue officer, unappealed, binds all co-sharers. The court interfered, displacing both decrees and ending the pre-emption case.",afb6d6386d5a1b79e00704571cfefafc2ce1cd5de7f0cb1faf38ffa47b9a3316
2200-2233,Civil Revision No. 3909 of 2016,2025-03-12,"
