Kabir/BO","The DEFENDANTS-PETITIONERS obtained under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 a Rule with status quo against the judgment and decree dated 07.11.2022 of the learned Additional District Judge, Lakshmipur, in Title Appeal No. 24 of 2016, modifying the decree of 24.04.2016 in Title Suit No. 338 of 2007 for partition of land in Tumchar and enlarging the PLAINTIFFS' saham. The shares, running from 1943 through the Bengal Alienation of Agricultural Land Act 1944, turned on 34 decimals sold in the famine to one PERSON_1 and claimed back in a redemption case before the Collector, Noakhali, closed conditionally on 15.11.1946; the plaintiffs bought those decimals in 1997. The PETITIONERS say the appellate court disbelieved a public record of presumptive value, misreading law and material, so the heirs' title revived and none passed to PERSON_1's heirs' purchasers. The OPPOSITE PARTIES answer that the condition went unmet.",Other: Bengal Alienation of Agricultural Land (Temporary Provisions) Act 1944,REFUSED,"The court weighed the 22 decimals claimed against shares for five defendants, two witnesses on one side, three on the other, exhibits aside; the moot point was payment of the sum fixed in 1946, the judgment on the section 4 application being conditional and unfulfilled, so the famine sale held, title passing lawfully to the buyers, while 28 DLR (AD) 61 settled that a record of right creates or extinguishes no title, leaving the khatian useless to the PETITIONERS, one of their own had parted with all she held. The court affirmed the appellate decree with shares of 62.87, 18, 6.64, 17, 5 decimals and none to defendant No. 7, discharging the Rule, vacating the stay, no costs.",03fed59c6b5f061c571baee5736bddbc2ecb3dd6f5104229c0e0ff0f8ad4548d
