","The PETITIONER, heir of PERSON_1, sued to declare, as procured by fraud behind his predecessors, the decree dated 17.11.2008 in Other Suit No. 38 of 2006; the suit failed at trial, the dismissal affirmed in appeal, and under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 he obtained a Rule against the decree dated 23.10.2017 of the learned Joint District Judge, 1st Court, Gaibandha. He says a Jamindar settlement of 1359 B.S. stood, State Acquisition and Tenancy Act 1950 misapplied in the khas recording, the 1987 decrees bound the Government, owning him as tenant, taking rent, publishing khatians, so the 1988 settlement was bad, no summons served, no reasons given, offending Order 20 rules 4 and 5. The RESPONDENTS answer that the decrees were ex parte, their predecessor pleaded them, contested the 2006 suit, then failed on limitation, a 2010 suit lapsing, so this suit was barred.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court held that Government, having admitted persons as tenants, taken rent and published Diyara, R.S. and B.R.S. khatians in their names, cannot afterwards call the land khas; title by declaration in Other Suit Nos. 63 and 112 of 1977, unchallenged, was thus acquired, yet the 1988 settlement issued without relief against those decrees or rectification; the 2006 decree, contested on the record, clouded them all, the 2009 appeal failed for delay, no revision followed, a later suit lapsed, the claim stood abandoned, so fresh proceedings after rejection were not open, rights having been intervened by the decree; judgments unhappily written, evidences undiscussed, disclosed no illegality; the Rule fell without costs, revision on condonation of delay left open.",d65ce5883d5b435ba26bd9ba37c2eef534c2c43436631dda731487e689702821
