Bench Officer","The PLAINTIFF-PETITIONERS obtained a Rule under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the order dated 24.03.2008 of the learned District Judge, Kishoregonj, in Miscellaneous Appeal No. 25 of 2008, staying the temporary injunction order dated 10.02.2008 of the Senior Assistant Judge in Other Class Suit No. 24 of 2007. The suit, for declaration of title to 70 decimals in C.S. plot No. 315, Khatian No. 246, pleads inheritance, a century of demarcated possession, rice mill, flower mill, godown and shops, and their names in the S.A. and R.S. records; opposite parties Nos. 5 and 6 claim the land as Government hat-bazar under section 20(2) of the State Acquisition and Tenancy Act 1950 and Ordinance No. 12 of 1967. They urge the stay application was unverified, unaffidavitted, without sufficient cause under Order 41 rule 5, heard on an off-date without notice, the order non-speaking.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"The court recorded that none appeared, though the opposite parties stood duly served, and that the appeal and the suit still lay pending below. No order having stayed the trial, the suit should have gone on, a declaration suit having nothing to do with an ad-interim injunction, the appellate court might itself have closed the appeal, seventeen years having passed with status quo kept. Ends of justice were met by disposing of the Rule with directions: status quo as to possession, and the nature and character of the land, to hold till the suit ends; Miscellaneous Appeal No. 25 of 2008, having lost its efficacy, to be closed on the District Judge's note; and the trial to conclude expeditiously, the suit being of 2007.",584a6ebc8a5104bbafe1e3a26a98d627b6703f45f78d65c938b4c845a8ef7d82
