","The DEFENDANT-PETITIONER obtained a Rule under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the decree dated 10.10.2021 of the learned Additional District Judge, 1st Court, Jhenaidah, in Title Appeal No. 09 of 2012, affirming the decree of 23.11.2011 of the learned Joint District Judge in Title Suit No. 50 of 2000, a partition suit over fifteen scheduled plots where shares went to the PLAINTIFFS and six groups of DEFENDANTS, none to her. She urges the plaintiffs never deposed nor authorised their sole witness, his evidence inadmissible; that her husband, a purchaser in the same land and a necessary party to partition on 28 DLR (AD) 5, was met with a sweeping remark; that her documents stood exhibited though the appellate court recorded none filed, offending Order 41 rule 31; and that papers held forged still carried a share.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The plaintiffs neither deposed nor authorised their sole witness; save husband and wife none may depose for another (9 CLR (AD) 206), the plaint case lying unproved. The PETITIONER's husband deposed as D.W.7 and produced registered deeds marked Ka-5, one further at appeal, without objection, yet the appellate court recorded that none came from her, betraying non-application of mind, the decree not conforming to Order 41 rule 31 (9 BLC (AD) 218). The necessary-party plea in a partition suit drew only a sweeping remark, and papers the trial court branded forged nonetheless bought a share. The Rule found merit, without costs; the appellate decree is displaced and the suit sent back for fresh disposal, both sides to prove their cases.",561f3a2b760e3e95e5f2348c00b7a1a0ed6f942ad07c5fd4fd5e877769dc201c
