","The PLAINTIFF-PETITIONERS obtained a Rule under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the decree dated 07.02.2022 of the learned Additional District Judge, 2nd Court, Bagerhat, in Title Appeal No. 02 of 2018, displacing the decree dated 27.04.2017 of the learned Senior Assistant Judge, Sadar, Bagerhat, in Title Suit No. 50 of 2003. Their predecessor's suit, that a partition decree obtained ex parte in Title Suit No. 199 of 1995, where he stood defendant No. 12, was fraudulently and collusively had without service and liable to be annulled, met the answer that summons stood duly served, the decree preliminary on 16.04.2002 and final on 06.11.2006, and that Order 9 rule 13, not a fresh suit, gave the remedy. They urge the burden of proving service lay on the DEFENDANTS and was wrongly shifted, no attesting witness or process server having been examined.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court held a separate suit lies to annul an ex parte decree got by fraud or suppression of summons, Order 9 rule 13 and the suit being concurrent remedies (II ADC (AD) 808; 31 DLR (AD) 51), so the suit stood maintainable. Two defence witnesses did not corroborate service, the process server and the attesting persons going unexamined, pointing to collusion in recording it, and the appellate finding that the process server and proforma witnesses had died rested on the peon's death alone. Due service unproved, the predecessor stood kept from appearing, the onus lying on the DEFENDANTS. The Rule found merit; the trial decree stands affirmed and Title Suit No. 199 of 1995 is to be restored to its original file and number.",b6e45bad13c96b7b30d956a10b6912f1123043ae489894a5a057875c9e8277b7
2250-2256,Civil Revision Number 66 of 1993,2025-02-27,"
