","The CO-SHARER-PETITIONERS, defendants 2 and 130 in the suit, obtained a Rule under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure 1908 against the decree dated 24.03.2021 of the learned Joint District Judge, 1st Court, Rangpur, in Other Class Appeal No. 37 of 2019, which partly succeeded for the appellants by enhancing their allotted share and displacing the preliminary partition decree dated 27.01.2019 of the learned Senior Assistant Judge, Mithapukur, Rangpur, in Other Class Suit No. 03 of 2003 decreeing the plaintiffs' claim in part. Genealogy and the C.S. and S.A. records stood admitted, and what was disputed was arithmetic: the parties' common predecessor had transferred by some twenty deeds more land than he owned, so nothing remained to inherit; and the petitioners' own purchases, the lands gifted to schools and to a mosque, and a 1989 gift deed went unaccounted below, the shares therefore running wrong by sataks.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"The parties' computation carried the day: the predecessor owned 8.6090 acres and transferred 8.87 acres, so plaintiff No. 1 and defendants 23 to 26 took nothing by inheritance, and defendant No. 22 took 0.6090 acre under the gift of 08.02.1989; defendant No. 2 inherited 3.0053 acres and bought 3.9673, and, having transferred 4.9907, was left with 1.9819 acres, or 2.2319 with the quarter-satak bought by defendant No. 130, against the 1.96 acres allotted; and a further .04402 satak gifted to a school fell out of the share of defendants 35 to 37, reducing them to 4.2022 acres. Counsel for the respondents prayed the Rule be disposed of on modification; the appellate decree was modified in those figures alone, the rest standing as below, without costs.",68e25664c3f66bd71604e158012be00cd42a340325c14454a0390933c9e35ac7
