","A SINGLE-CONSIGNMENT PETITIONER brought hot rolled steel sheet from China under a letter of credit of 24.02.2022, filed bill of entry C-1002116 on 06.06.2022 and had the goods finally assessed on 09.06.2022 at Tk. 30,13,981.40 in taxes. When it pressed for release it was told that a bank guarantee must first come in, and on its application of 26.06.2022 for a chemical examination and for provisional release the respondents took guarantee No. 1123220004 of 27.06.2022 for Tk. 31,57,019.31, the goods then going free. The importer obtained a rule nisi under Article 102(2)(a)(i) and (ii) of the Constitution against that provisional assessment, with a restraint on encashment; the Board answers that the declaration understated the quality, that the importer chose the course, and that the writ comes too early.",Other: Customs Act 1969,ALLOWED,"Here the sequence was decisive: entry on 06.06.2022, final assessment on 09.06.2022, then, only after the petitioner applied on 26.06.2022 for a test and for release against a continuing guarantee, the security of Tk. 31,57,019.31 taken on 27.06.2022. The Act, the bench held, knows provisional assessment only where duty cannot immediately be assessed; once assessment is done the officer's tools are section 80(2) re-assessment, section 83A amendment or section 32 proceedings, and a demand beyond those routes wants lawful authority. The importer's request, the compulsion pleaded and the equitable bars pressed by the Crown gave way to that want of power, estoppel lying against no statute. The rule took effect, the guarantee to be returned, the respondents free to proceed by law.",b907a63115c227d62059fae293bf8c9e1f818ab5f4724db41db5bf5148432372
