","THE IMPORTER-PETITIONER brought hot rolled steel sheet from China under a letter of credit of 24.02.2022, presented bill of entry C-1020639 on 08.06.2022 and had the consignment finally assessed that same day at Tk. 36,55,610.92 in taxes. Release nonetheless withheld, the respondents moved the importer to apply on 26.06.2022 for a chemical examination and for provisional release against security, and guarantee No. 1123220006 of 29.06.2022 for Tk. 38,29,594.18 came in before the goods went. The importer obtained a rule nisi under Article 102(2)(a)(i) and (ii) of the Constitution declaring that doing without lawful authority and ordering the guarantee back, together with a restraint on encashment; the Board answers mis-declaration of quality, the petitioner's own prayer for the course taken, prematurity and unclean hands.",Other: Customs Act 1969,ALLOWED,"The dates carried the case: entry and final assessment fell on the same day, 08.06.2022, the demand for security coming three weeks later on an application the petitioner itself filed on 26.06.2022. Section 81 of the Customs Act, 1969 presupposes that duty cannot at once be assessed; once assessed, the statute leaves section 80(2) re-assessment, section 83A amendment or section 32 proceedings, and nothing permits a fresh provisional demand on a closed file. Prematurity, unclean hands and delay were met by the prior question, the respondents having no power to act at all; the mis-declaration was theirs to determine. Relief followed the rule, the guarantee to go back, the respondents free to proceed under the Act.",ab367f2d2ea1e07a6e3ba8708f3aee9e876ccc4cf14bbc9f8617e721e8fcc077
