","THE SAME PETITIONER MANUFACTURER's second consignment, four sizes of hot rolled steel coil from Korea under one letter of credit of 04.04.2022 and a proforma invoice of 09.11.2020, was entered on 26.04.2022 under bill of entry C-785968 and finally assessed on 19.05.2022 at Tk. 1,67,82,730.14 in taxes, the commercial invoice showing USD 124,072.96. Before adjudication the customs respondents imposed a provisional assessment and took bank guarantee No. 04/2022 of 20.06.2022 for Tk. 1,30,38,787.12 against the importer's own application for release, the goods going free on it. The importer moved this Court under Article 102(2)(a)(i) and (ii) of the Constitution to have that proceeding declared without lawful authority and the guarantee returned; the Board answered mis-declaration, the petitioner's request, prematurity and unclean hands.",Other: Customs Act 1969,ALLOWED,"This fell with the companion matters on the same short point: once an assessment stood complete under section 80 of the Customs Act, 1969, the authority might re-assess under section 80(2), amend under section 83A or prosecute under section 32, but not revert to section 81, open only where duty cannot immediately be assessed. The security taken, Tk. 1,30,38,787.12 against taxes of Tk. 1,67,82,730.14, and the 2020 invoice behind a 2022 credit, went to valuation's merits, left to the statute's machinery. Consent could not cure the want of power, estoppel being unavailable to validate what the law forbids. The rule succeeded in full, the guarantee to be returned, the respondents at liberty to proceed in accordance with law.",37011029de939641023ecdad28411601105119497669e14ccde8250e6ecb2ae1
